# YouTube & Media Support

SlideDeckML supports **YouTube videos**, regular videos, and images!

===

# YouTube Videos

Simply use the standard markdown image syntax with a YouTube URL:

![YouTube Demo](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ)

===

# YouTube Short URLs

You can also use YouTube short URLs (youtu.be):

![Another Video](https://youtu.be/dQw4w9WgXcQ)

===

# YouTube Embed URLs

Or even direct embed URLs:

![Embed Format](https://www.youtube.com/embed/dQw4w9WgXcQ)

===

# Styled YouTube Videos

You can apply styling to YouTube embeds:

::: {text-align: 'center'}
![Centered Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ)
:::

===

# Multiple Videos

You can add multiple videos to a slide:

::: {display: 'inline-block'; width: '45%'; margin: '10px'}
![Video 1](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ)
:::

::: {display: 'inline-block'; width: '45%'; margin: '10px'}
![Video 2](https://youtu.be/dQw4w9WgXcQ)
:::

===

# Images Still Work

Regular images work as before:

![Placeholder Image](https://placehold.co/600x400)

===

# Mixed Media

Combine images and YouTube videos:

![Image](https://placehold.co/400x300)

![YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ)

===

# With Animations

YouTube embeds work with fragment animations:

::: {animate: "fade-up"}
![Animated YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ)
:::

===

